                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 12,
                "retweet_count": 3,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I support the continuing resolution to keep the government open. \n\nWith costs already shooting through the roof for families in Southwest Washington and across our country, I could not in good conscience vote to shut our government down, which would have made health care and food even more expensive for millions of Americans while handing the executive branch even more control over the nuts and bolts of the administrative apparatus. \n\nIf you\u2019re worried about families losing SNAP benefits and going hungry, research into cancer treatments for kids getting cut, or overworked air traffic controllers, you should be really concerned about the can of worms that a government shutdown would crack open.\n\nIt\u2019s now been more than a year since Congress has passed an actual government funding bill. Continuing resolutions are the bare minimum \u2013 we were sent here to do more than just keep the lights on. \n\nAs we enter the next round of budget negotiations, I\u2019ll keep fighting as a member of the House Appropriations Committee for a real, bipartisan appropriations process that protects Americans\u2019 health care and builds an economy where folks only need to work one job to raise a family.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1758297800,
                "view_count": 30015
            },
